      "page_title": "Coroutines, Tasks and the Event Loop",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. Coroutine vs Task",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`async def f()`: calling `f()` returns a ==coroutine object==",
            "The body runs **only** once it is awaited or scheduled",
            "A ==Task== wraps a coroutine and schedules it on the loop",
            "A Task runs __concurrently__ with the caller that created it"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def fetch():",
            "    print('running')",
            "coro = fetch()  # prints nothing",
            "await coro      # prints now"
          ],
          "note": "calling is not running"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Task method",
            "Gives you"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`.done()`",
              "finished yet?"
            ],
            [
              "`.result()`",
              "return value"
            ],
            [
              "`.exception()`",
              "raised error"
            ],
            [
              "`.cancel()` / `.cancelled()`",
              "request / check"
            ],
            [
              "`add_done_callback(fn)`",
              "run fn when done"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Task is a **subclass** of ==Future==, so it has the whole Future API shown above."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How the loop switches",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The event loop is ==single-threaded== and cooperative",
            "Tasks switch **only** at an `await` that really suspends",
            "`await a(); await b()` runs inline, one after another",
            "A blocking call freezes __every__ task on the loop"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Blocks the loop",
            "Use instead"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`time.sleep(1)`",
              "`await asyncio.sleep(1)`"
            ],
            [
              "CPU-heavy loop",
              "`await asyncio.to_thread(f)`"
            ],
            [
              "blocking I/O call",
              "`await asyncio.to_thread(f)`"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "create loop",
                "sub": "asyncio.run(main())",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "run main",
                "sub": "to completion"
              },
              {
                "text": "cancel pending",
                "sub": "leftover tasks",
                "ink": "orange"
              },
              {
                "text": "close loop",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Introspection",
          "items": [
            "`asyncio.current_task()` → the ==running Task==",
            "`asyncio.all_tasks()` → set of tasks **not done**"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: 2s vs 1s",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def main():  # sequential",
            "    await sleep(1)",
            "    await sleep(1)  # total 2s"
          ],
          "note": "no overlap: plain awaits"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def main():  # tasks",
            "    t1 = create_task(sleep(1))",
            "    t2 = create_task(sleep(1))",
            "    await t1; await t2  # 1s"
          ],
          "note": "both sleeps overlap"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Style",
            "Total time"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "two plain awaits",
              "2s"
            ],
            [
              "two Tasks",
              "__1s__"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`fetch()` with no await → warns ==coroutine ... was never awaited==",
            "…and the work **never** runs at all",
            "Expecting `await a(); await b()` to run concurrently",
            "`time.sleep()` inside `async def` stalls all tasks"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Rule of thumb",
          "text": "`await` = wait for a result. Task = run it **alongside**."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
