    {
      "page_title": "create_task and Keeping References",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What create_task Does"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`create_task(coro, *, name=None, context=None)`",
            "Schedules coro on the ==running loop==",
            "Returns a `Task` **at once**, without waiting for it",
            "Body starts at the caller's **next** `await`"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def main():",
            "    t = asyncio.create_task(job())",
            "    print('job not started yet')",
            "    await asyncio.sleep(0)",
            "    # job() starts running here"
          ],
          "note": "starts at next await, not create_task"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. Weak References & GC"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Holder",
            "Ref",
            "Task survives?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "event loop",
              "weak",
              "{red:no}"
            ],
            [
              "local variable",
              "strong",
              "while in scope"
            ],
            [
              "set + discard",
              "strong",
              "until done"
            ],
            [
              "TaskGroup",
              "strong",
              "{green:yes}"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Loop keeps only ==weak refs== to tasks",
            "No strong ref → task can be **garbage-collected** mid-run",
            "Never-awaited error logged only at GC",
            "Log line: `Task exception was never retrieved`"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Fire-and-Forget Fix"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "background = set()",
            "t = asyncio.create_task(c())",
            "background.add(t)",
            "t.add_done_callback(",
            "    background.discard)"
          ],
          "note": "set holds strong ref until done"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "name= and context=",
          "items": [
            "`name='mailer'` or `t.set_name()` → readable debug output",
            "Named tasks show up in `asyncio.all_tasks()` dumps",
            "`context=` (3.11+) runs in a given `contextvars.Context`",
            "Default: task gets a ==copy== of the current context"
          ],
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. Eager Tasks (3.12+)"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "loop = asyncio.get_running_loop()",
            "loop.set_task_factory(",
            "    asyncio.eager_task_factory)"
          ],
          "note": "runs sync until first suspension"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==eager_task_factory== runs the task **synchronously** at first",
            "Keeps running until its first real suspension",
            "Saves one loop iteration per task"
          ],
          "style": "check"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common Mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`asyncio.create_task(send_email())` discarded → can **vanish**",
            "Assuming the task starts inside create_task",
            "Never awaiting → error only surfaces at GC",
            "Unnamed tasks → `Task-17` in all_tasks() dumps"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Prefer TaskGroup.create_task",
          "text": "The ==group== holds the reference and **awaits** the task for you. No lost tasks and no silent errors (see page 4)."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "spawning tasks safely"
    },
