    {
      "page_title": "Exception Groups and except* Matching",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is an ExceptionGroup",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==ExceptionGroup(msg, [excs])==: PEP 654, Python 3.11",
            "Carries several **unrelated** exceptions at once",
            "`.exceptions` holds the leaves as a tuple",
            "==BaseExceptionGroup== is the base class",
            "ExceptionGroup holds only `Exception` subclasses"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "eg = ExceptionGroup(\"batch\", [",
            "    ValueError(\"bad id\"),",
            "    TypeError(\"not str\")])",
            "eg.exceptions  # 2-tuple of leaves"
          ],
          "note": "BaseException leaves need BaseExceptionGroup"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How except* matches",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`except* ValueError as eg:` takes the ValueError **leaves**",
            "`eg` is an ExceptionGroup holding only those leaves",
            "Several except* clauses can run, one per matching type",
            "Plain `except` runs at most **one** clause",
            "Leftover leaves are re-raised as a ==smaller group=="
          ],
          "style": "number",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Group raised",
            "except* V / T",
            "Result"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "[V, T]",
              "both run",
              "all handled"
            ],
            [
              "[V, KeyError]",
              "V runs",
              "{red:KeyError group} re-raised"
            ],
            [
              "[V(a), V(b)]",
              "V runs once",
              "`eg` has 2 leaves"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 1,
          "frame": "solid"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. subgroup, split, nesting",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "vals = eg.subgroup(",
            "    lambda e: isinstance(",
            "        e, ValueError))",
            "m, rest = eg.split(ValueError)",
            "# m: V leaves  rest: the others"
          ],
          "note": "either half may be None"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "==subgroup(pred)== keeps only the matching leaves",
            "==split(pred)== returns a `(match, rest)` pair",
            "Groups can **nest**: a leaf can be another group",
            "Tracebacks print a __tree__ of every sub-exception"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "text",
          "lines": [
            "ExceptionGroup: run (2)",
            "+-+-- 1 --",
            "  | ValueError: bad id",
            "  +-- 2 --",
            "  | ExceptionGroup: io (1)",
            "  +-+-- 1 -- TimeoutError"
          ],
          "note": "each +-- is a leaf or subgroup"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`except ValueError` **misses** a group that holds a ValueError",
            "Common TaskGroup trap: child errors always arrive wrapped",
            "Using `except` and `except*` in one try → SyntaxError",
            "`break` / `continue` / `return` in except* → SyntaxError",
            "ExceptionGroup built with a BaseException → TypeError"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "TaskGroup rule",
          "text": "Wrap `async with TaskGroup()` in ==try / except*==, never a plain except."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Bare ValueError too",
          "text": "`except* ValueError` also catches a **plain** ValueError: it is wrapped in a group of one."
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "PEP 654 error trees"
