    {
      "page_title": "Cancellation: cancel() and CancelledError",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "★ 1. What is cancel()?",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`task.cancel(msg=None)` ==requests== cancellation; it does not stop the task at once",
            "==CancelledError== is thrown into the coroutine at its **next** await",
            "Returns `False` if the task is already done, otherwise `True`",
            "`True` means the request was made, not that the task has stopped",
            "`CancelledError` subclasses ==BaseException== (since 3.8), so `except Exception` misses it"
          ],
          "style": "dot",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Call",
            "Result",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`cancel()` on running",
              "`True`",
              "request only"
            ],
            [
              "`cancel()` on done",
              "`False`",
              "no-op"
            ],
            [
              "`cancelled()`",
              "`True`",
              "ended by **CancelledError**"
            ],
            [
              "`await t` (cancelled)",
              "raises",
              "CancelledError in the awaiter"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "★ 2. Mechanism",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "t.cancel()",
                "sub": "returns True",
                "ink": "blue"
              },
              {
                "text": "next await",
                "sub": "task resumes"
              },
              {
                "text": "CancelledError",
                "sub": "thrown inside",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "finally: cleanup",
                "sub": "then re-raise",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "cancelled() == True",
                "sub": "awaiter gets error",
                "ink": "purple"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`task.cancelling()` (3.11) = the ==number of pending== cancel requests",
            "`task.uncancel()` **decrements** that count by one",
            "==TaskGroup== and `asyncio.timeout` use both to tell their own cancel from an outside one",
            "Count still > 0 after uncancel → the outside cancel propagates"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Step",
            "Event",
            "cancelling()"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "1",
              "`timeout()` deadline hits → cancel",
              "1"
            ],
            [
              "2",
              "shutdown also calls `t.cancel()`",
              "2"
            ],
            [
              "3",
              "timeout exits → `uncancel()`",
              "1"
            ],
            [
              "4",
              "count > 0 → CancelledError, not TimeoutError",
              "__1__"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 3,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "t = asyncio.create_task(poll())",
            "...",
            "t.cancel()        # just a request",
            "try:",
            "    await t       # wait until it ends",
            "except asyncio.CancelledError:",
            "    pass          # expected: stopped"
          ],
          "note": "the standard way to stop background tasks"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Cleanup template",
          "text": "`except CancelledError:` → `cleanup()` → `raise`. Catch it only to tidy up, and **always** re-raise."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Remember",
          "text": "Cancel, then await. Clean up in `finally`, never swallow the error. Shielding is on page 7 and timeouts on page 8."
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`msg=` labels ==why== the task was cancelled",
            "Shows up in the traceback and `e.args`",
            "Handy when many callers may cancel one task"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "stopping tasks safely"
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cancellation Mistakes & Cleanup Patterns",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "★ 4. Common mistakes",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`except CancelledError: pass` inside the task → the task **ignores** the cancel",
            "Swallowing it breaks ==TaskGroup==, `timeout()` and app shutdown",
            "Expecting `except Exception` to catch it: it's a BaseException",
            "Reading `cancel()` → `True` as \"the task has already stopped\"",
            "A task that swallowed the cancel and returned has `cancelled()` == `False`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "★ 3. Example",
          "ink": "purple"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "async def poll():",
            "    try:",
            "        while True:",
            "            await tick()",
            "    finally:",
            "        await close_conn()  # cleanup"
          ],
          "note": "finally runs on cancel too"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "★ 5. cancel(msg)",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "t.cancel('shutdown')",
            "try:",
            "    await t",
            "except CancelledError as e:",
            "    print(e.args)  # ('shutdown',)"
          ],
          "note": "msg rides on the CancelledError"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "★ 6. Stopping many tasks",
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "for t in tasks:",
            "    t.cancel()",
            "await gather(*tasks,",
            "    return_exceptions=True)"
          ],
          "note": "waits until every task has ended"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "★ 7. Handler patterns",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Pattern",
            "Cancel works?"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`finally: cleanup()`",
              "{green:yes}"
            ],
            [
              "`except CE: cleanup(); raise`",
              "{green:yes}"
            ],
            [
              "`except CE: pass`",
              "{red:no}: swallowed"
            ],
            [
              "`except Exception:`",
              "not caught at all"
            ]
          ],
          "highlightRow": 0,
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Checklist",
          "items": [
            "Cancel, then ==await== the task",
            "Cleanup in `finally`",
            "**Always** re-raise CancelledError"
          ],
          "ink": "purple"
        }
      ],
      "hero": "python",
      "subtitle": "stopping tasks safely"
