    {
      "page_title": "asyncio.shield",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "1. What is shield?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "`await asyncio.shield(aw)` protects the ==inner awaitable== from being cancelled when the **outer** task is cancelled.",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Outer `await` still raises `CancelledError`",
            "Inner task keeps **running** to completion",
            "No guard against `inner.cancel()` called directly"
          ],
          "style": "dot"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "2. How it works"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              {
                "text": "outer.cancel()",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "await shield(t)",
                "sub": "raises CancelledError",
                "ink": "red"
              },
              {
                "text": "inner t",
                "sub": "keeps running",
                "ink": "green"
              },
              {
                "text": "t.result()",
                "sub": "work finished",
                "ink": "green"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Keep a reference!",
          "items": [
            "shield wraps a coroutine in a ==Task==",
            "Loop holds only weak refs (see p.2)",
            "No strong ref to `t` → may be **GC'd**"
          ],
          "ink": "orange"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Example: safe commit"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "DB ==commit== must not tear half-way",
            "Payment write: charge + record land together"
          ],
          "style": "star"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "t = create_task(commit())",
            "try:",
            "    await shield(t)",
            "except CancelledError:",
            "    await t  # let commit finish",
            "    raise    # still cancelled"
          ],
          "note": "always re-raise after commit lands"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "4. shield vs try/finally"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "",
            "shield",
            "try/finally"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Cancellation",
              "**hidden** from inner",
              "delivered"
            ],
            [
              "Inner work",
              "keeps running",
              "stops at await"
            ],
            [
              "Cleanup",
              "not needed",
              "runs **after** cancel"
            ],
            [
              "Use for",
              "must-finish writes",
              "release resources"
            ]
          ],
          "frame": "dashed"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Common mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Shielding **everything** → uncancellable ==zombies==",
            "Zombies block shutdown and TaskGroup exit",
            "Dropping the ref: shielded task GC'd mid-run",
            "Assuming shield stops `inner.cancel()`"
          ],
          "style": "cross",
          "frame": "dashed",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "shield ≠ durability",
          "text": "At shutdown `asyncio.run` still **cancels** leftover shielded tasks, so use a real transaction for durability."
        }
